  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> intersect at <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> in the first quadrant. If <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;units, then the square of the distance of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> from the origin is equal to"
